---
/**
 * agentpod.dev.
 *
 * Rewritten on 2026-09-12. The previous page was audited against the code and
 * could not be published: its waitlist form discarded the address and told the
 * visitor "we'll be in touch"; it offered .msi, .deb, .rpm and .AppImage
 * installers that are not built (releases are raw Go binaries for linux and
 * darwin, and there is no Windows target at all); it listed iOS and Android apps
 * as "coming soon" when no mobile app exists; and its features table sold
 * "container flavors", a concept dropped from the schema in migration 0023.
 *
 * Everything here is checked against the code. The harness list is
 * `registerDescriptors` in cmd/agentpod-node/registry.go; the capabilities are the
 * hub's `gateCapability` calls plus the console's station panels; the provisioning
 * substrates are the driver files in services/provisioner/; the install command is
 * what install.sh actually accepts. If those move, this page is wrong.
 *
 * The hero is a fleet panel rather than a headline over a gradient, because the
 * product's thesis is that machines you cannot reach are still reachable: every
 * node dials OUT, so a laptop behind CGNAT is in the fleet on the same terms as a
 * VPS. Showing that is the argument.
 */
const harnesses = ['Hermes', 'OpenClaw', 'Claude Code', 'Codex', 'OpenCode', 'Pi'];
const substrates = ['Docker', 'Cloudflare', 'Modal', 'Fly'];

const nodes = [
  {
    name: 'workhorse',
    kind: 'VPS · Ubuntu',
    state: 'online',
    stations: [
      { name: 'hermes', detail: 'coder-kai · hanuman' },
      { name: 'claude-code', detail: 'billing-api' },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'mba-priya',
    kind: 'laptop · behind CGNAT',
    state: 'online',
    stations: [{ name: 'codex', detail: 'design-system' }],
  },
  {
    name: 'pod-7f3a',
    kind: 'provisioned · Docker',
    state: 'idle',
    stations: [{ name: 'opencode', detail: 'nightly-sweep' }],
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>AgentPod — the console for the machines your agents live on</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A fleet and facilities console for agent runtimes. Attach to the agents you already run, reach machines behind NAT, and manage files, logs, terminals, health and cleanup from one place. Self-hostable."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400;12..96,600;12..96,800&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --ink: #101c2b;
        --raised: #18293c;
        --raised-2: #21374e;
        --line: #2c4560;
        --text: #eef4fa;
        --muted: #93a8bf;
        --cyan: #5fb3d4;
        --green: #63c9a0;
        --display: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif;
        --body: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
        --mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
      }

      /* Light, for a visitor whose system asks for it. The docs site follows the
         reader's preference, so a dark-only page here would mean a dark landing
         page and light docs — the mismatch worth avoiding. */
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
        :root {
          --ink: #fbfcfe;
          --raised: #eef3f8;
          --raised-2: #e0e9f2;
          --line: #ccdae7;
          --text: #101c29;
          --muted: #4b6076;
          --cyan: #1d6c8c;
          --green: #1c7a5b;
        }
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      .wrap { width: 100%; max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }

      header.mast .wrap {
        display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
        padding-top: 26px; padding-bottom: 26px; gap: 20px;
      }
      .brand {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 800; font-size: 21px;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--text); text-decoration: none;
      }
      .brand span { color: var(--cyan); }
      nav { display: flex; gap: 22px; font-size: 15px; }
      nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
      nav a:hover, nav a:focus-visible { color: var(--text); }

      .hero .wrap {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 60px; align-items: center;
        padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 84px;
      }
      h1 {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 800;
        font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 4.8vw, 3.7rem); line-height: 1.05;
        letter-spacing: -0.035em; margin: 0 0 20px; text-wrap: balance;
      }
      h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--cyan); }
      .lede { font-size: 1.14rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 30px; max-width: 31em; }
      .actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .btn {
        display: inline-block; padding: 13px 22px; border-radius: 9px;
        font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; text-decoration: none;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
      }
      .btn-primary { background: var(--cyan); color: var(--ink); }
      .btn-primary:hover { filter: brightness(1.1); }
      .btn-ghost { border-color: var(--line); color: var(--text); }
      .btn-ghost:hover { border-color: var(--cyan); }

      /* ── the fleet panel: this page's signature ─────────────────── */
      .fleet {
        background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 15px; overflow: hidden;
      }
      .fleet-head {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; padding: 13px 16px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted);
      }
      .fleet-head b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
      .fleet-body { padding: 6px 0; }
      .node { padding: 11px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .node:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
      .node-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; }
      .led { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; flex: none; }
      .led.online { background: var(--green); }
      .led.idle { background: var(--muted); }
      .node-name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }
      .node-kind { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin-left: auto; }
      .stations { margin: 8px 0 0 16px; padding-left: 12px; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .station { display: flex; gap: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; padding: 3px 0; }
      .station .s-name { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--cyan); }
      .station .s-detail { color: var(--muted); }
      .fleet-foot {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 11px 16px;
        font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted);
      }

      section.band { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      section.band .wrap { padding-top: 68px; padding-bottom: 68px; }
      h2 {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600;
        font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3vw, 2.05rem); letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        margin: 0 0 14px; text-wrap: balance;
      }
      .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 36px; max-width: 62ch; }
      .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 26px; }
      .cell h3 {
        font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600;
        margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      }
      .cell p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15.5px; }

      pre {
        background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 15px 17px; overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 14px;
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text);
      }
      pre .c { color: var(--muted); }
      .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14.5px; margin: 0; }

      .chips { display: flex; gap: 9px; flex-wrap: wrap; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
      .chips li {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--text);
        border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 7px; padding: 7px 13px;
        background: var(--raised);
      }

      footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      footer .wrap {
        display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;
        padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 44px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--muted);
      }
      footer a { color: var(--muted); }
      footer a:hover { color: var(--text); }
      .fnav { display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

      @media (max-width: 860px) {
        .hero .wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; padding-bottom: 56px; }
        .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
      }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        * { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="mast">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="brand" href="/">agent<span>pod</span></a>
        <nav>
          <a href="https://docs.agentpod.dev">Docs</a>
          <a href="/blog">Blog</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/SuperJackfruitLabs/agentpod">Source</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div>
          <h1>The console for the machines your agents <em>live on</em>.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Your agents run somewhere — a server, a laptop, a container you spun up last week.
            AgentPod is where you see those places and reach into them: files, logs, a terminal,
            health, cleanup. Point it at what you already run.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://docs.agentpod.dev/start/first-node/">Enroll a node</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://docs.agentpod.dev">Read the docs</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Signature element. See the note at the top of this file. -->
        <div class="fleet" role="img"
          aria-label="A fleet: three nodes — a VPS, a laptop behind CGNAT, and a provisioned Docker container — each listing the harness stations running on it. All are reachable because every node dials out to the hub.">
          <div class="fleet-head">
            <b>Fleet</b><span>3 nodes · 4 stations</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fleet-body">
            {nodes.map((n) => (
              <div class="node">
                <div class="node-row">
                  <span class={`led ${n.state}`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="node-name">{n.name}</span>
                  <span class="node-kind">{n.kind}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="stations">
                  {n.stations.map((s) => (
                    <div class="station">
                      <span class="s-name">{s.name}</span>
                      <span class="s-detail">{s.detail}</span>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="fleet-foot">
            Every node dials <strong>out</strong>. No inbound ports — which is why the laptop is
            in the fleet on the same terms as the VPS.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Attach to what you already run</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          AgentPod does not run your agents and does not ask you to move them. It ships a
          descriptor per harness that knows how to ask that harness what it is running, where its
          config and logs live, and how to start and stop it — wrapping each one's native
          interface rather than reinventing it.
        </p>
        <ul class="chips">{harnesses.map((h) => <li>{h}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>What you can do to a runtime</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          Each operation is gated on a capability the station declares. A request for one it has
          not declared is refused at the hub, before anything reaches the machine.
        </p>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>Files, logs, terminal</h3>
            <p>Browse and edit the workspace, tail logs live, open a real shell — brokered through
              the hub, executed by the local agent.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>Health and lifecycle</h3>
            <p>What a station reports about itself, and start, stop or restart. Every action is
              written to the audit trail before it is dispatched, not after.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>Cleanup and changesets</h3>
            <p>Plan a disk reclaim and inspect the plan before applying it. See what an agent has
              actually changed in its working tree.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Enrolling a machine</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          One command on the target host. It downloads the right binary, installs a service, and
          enrolls with your hub.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="c"># linux and macOS, amd64 and arm64</span>
curl -fsSL https://github.com/SuperJackfruitLabs/agentpod/releases/latest/download/install.sh \
  | sudo bash -s -- https://hub.example.com &lt;TOKEN&gt;</code></pre>
        <p class="note">
          Without root, pass <code>--user</code> to install under your login session instead.
          Binaries are published for linux and darwin on amd64 and arm64.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Check a machine before you trust it</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          <code>apn scan</code> checks the agent runtimes on a host for the two ways they get
          taken over: a listener bound to every interface, and credential files other users can
          read. It needs no hub, no account and no network, and exits 0, 1 or 2 so it works in
          cron.
        </p>
        <pre><code>apn scan</code></pre>
        <p class="note">
          A check that cannot determine an answer says so. It is never reported as a pass.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Or let it provision the machine</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          When there is nothing to attach to yet, AgentPod can create the runtime and enroll it for
          you, on any of these.
        </p>
        <ul class="chips">{substrates.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>You host all of it</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          The hub is a Bun service over Postgres. The console is a static site. The node agent is a
          single Go binary. There is no account here to sign up for — clone it, run it, and the
          fleet is yours.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://docs.agentpod.dev">Read the docs</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/SuperJackfruitLabs/agentpod">View the source</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap">
        <span>AgentPod · self-hosted · MIT</span>
        <span class="fnav">
          <a href="https://docs.agentpod.dev">Documentation</a>
          <a href="/blog">Blog</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/SuperJackfruitLabs/agentpod">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://docs.kaambaan.dev">kaambaan</a>
          <a href="https://docs.supermessage.dev">supermessage</a>
        </span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
